From: fab <faibiantorrestech@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:44:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backup: keep patcher settings in a vanilla-safe section
 (inkOS-Patcher)

Full backups and theme exports move every setting the patches add into
one nested "inkos_patcher" section ({format, prefs, overrides}). Vanilla
inkOS's importer skips nested values, so a patched backup restores
cleanly on vanilla with stock behavior.

Vanilla keys whose patched value would look wrong in vanilla get a
vanilla-safe value at the top level and the real one under "overrides".
Today that is HOME_PAGES_NUM: with a custom page layout (empty pages,
uneven pages) vanilla gets the number of non-empty pages, so it shows
the same apps in the same order, split evenly, with no empty pages.

The patched importer runs vanilla's import, then restores the section
(known keys only, with their types). Older patched backups, with
patcher keys at the top level, still import as before. Logic lives in
data/PatcherBackup.kt; Prefs.kt gets four one-line hooks.

